title: Accept or cleanly refuse durations with a leading zero
created: 2026-09-24T22:57:36Z
updated: 2026-09-24T22:57:36Z
effort: S
area: cli
handoff:

duration_seconds (bin/pidly:199-213) only checks for digits, so
PIDLY_LEASE=08s reaches $((08 * 1)) and the shell prints "Illegal number: 08"
before pidly's own message. Strip leading zeros (or refuse them) before the
arithmetic, for PIDLY_LEASE and list --stale alike.
